WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.233
- All right,

00:00:01.233 --> 00:00:02.066
So we just sit down.

00:00:02.066 --> 00:00:02.940
- We're just gonna sit down.

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.380
- Okay, I've never done this.

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:05.390
I'm so intrigued.

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:06.450
I've never done anything like this.

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:07.570
- Okay, great.

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:08.453
So.

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:13.750
So there is a mother
energy that is present.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:15.380
So, if you're mom is not departed,

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.360
it would be like a grandmother or an aunt

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:19.110
or someone that was like a mother to you.

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:20.930
- It could literally be any of those--

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:21.788
- [Theresa] Oh!
- 'Cause everyone died

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:23.045
before me, so.

00:00:23.045 --> 00:00:23.878
(laughing)

00:00:23.878 --> 00:00:24.711
- Oh, okay, but--
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:24.711 --> 00:00:26.040
- But you're mom is here
in the physical world?

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.300
- My mom is alive, yeah.
- Okay, you're very fortunate

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.390
because you have not lost
a lot of people here in

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:31.223
the physical world.

00:00:31.223 --> 00:00:33.740
- Yeah, I don't know many
people that have passed away.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:34.595
- [Theresa] Right.
- So, yeah.

00:00:34.595 --> 00:00:36.360
- Well, can I talk about
the dad that's departed?

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:37.600
- Oh, my dad did die?

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:38.567
Oh, I don't know him.

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:39.540
- Oh!
- Oh, yeah.

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:40.550
I'm sorry.
- Oh, okay.

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:41.987
- I was just going to ask you about pie?

00:00:41.987 --> 00:00:42.940
- I love pie.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:43.870
- That's what they told me.
- [Kelly] Oh!

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:44.703
- They go,

00:00:44.703 --> 00:00:45.581
"Kelly loves pie."

00:00:45.581 --> 00:00:46.414
- Oh, I love pie!
- Because, I'm like,

00:00:46.414 --> 00:00:47.370
they showed me cherry pie and I'm,

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:48.203
like, okay.

00:00:48.203 --> 00:00:49.036
What am I supposed to say with that?

00:00:49.036 --> 00:00:49.869
I'm don't have a--

00:00:49.869 --> 00:00:50.702
- Oh, that's funny.

00:00:50.702 --> 00:00:52.050
Cherry pie is my sister's thing.

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:52.883
- Okay.
- But she's the one

00:00:52.883 --> 00:00:54.790
he probably is trying to talk to.

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:55.623
- Well, listen.

00:00:55.623 --> 00:00:56.650
- We don't know each other.

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:57.980
- But you have understand,

00:00:57.980 --> 00:00:59.990
your dad could not take responsibility

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:01.040
for things in his life,

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:02.900
here in the physical world.
- Not a one.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:04.617
- His soul is stepping forward and saying,

00:01:04.617 --> 00:01:06.067
"I know what you felt.

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:08.530
"I know what you went through
and for that I am sorry."

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:09.730
So...
- Oh, I've already forgiven.

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:10.563
So, I'm good.

00:01:10.563 --> 00:01:11.396
But I'm not, like,

00:01:11.396 --> 00:01:12.380
mad at it, if he can hear me.
- No.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:13.430
- Oh, I was like...
- No, no, no.

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:14.880
Like, that's not what this is about.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:15.713
- Okay.

00:01:15.713 --> 00:01:16.960
- You have to understand,
it's where someone,

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:19.260
if they hurt us or disappoint us,

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:20.590
only if the soul has learned

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:23.050
the lesson to see things differently,

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:24.430
they can come through and say that.

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:25.263
So...

00:01:25.263 --> 00:01:26.096
- All right.

00:01:26.096 --> 00:01:27.710
- That's all.
- I'll tell my sister.

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:31.880
- For your dad to be able to come through.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:32.713
- Oh, yeah,

00:01:32.713 --> 00:01:33.770
Candice did lose someone, yes.

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:34.603
- Who are you?

00:01:34.603 --> 00:01:36.010
- [Candice] I'm Candice.
- [Kelly] She's my stylist.

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:36.843
- Oh, hi.

00:01:36.843 --> 00:01:37.770
Nice to meet you.
- So nice to meet you.

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:38.603
- Oh my God!

00:01:38.603 --> 00:01:39.510
The very first thing you said was mother

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:40.680
and I thinking my life.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:42.300
But her mother recently passed.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.540
That's right.

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:44.373
- [Candice] Yeah.

00:01:44.373 --> 00:01:45.206
- Yeah.

00:01:45.206 --> 00:01:46.235
- Were you watching her breath in the end?

00:01:46.235 --> 00:01:47.620
- Yeah.
- [Theresa] Okay.

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:49.697
- So you're mom just said to me, she says,

00:01:49.697 --> 00:01:52.237
"Please tell my daughter, I
know how much she misses me."

00:01:52.237 --> 00:01:53.070
- I do.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:56.450
- So know that you're mom is showing me

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.730
the breath--
- Oh my God!

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:00.610
- And watching you breath.

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:01.610
- I watched her.

00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:02.443
- So she says,

00:02:02.443 --> 00:02:04.587
"Please, I wanna thank you
for releasing my soul here in

00:02:04.587 --> 00:02:06.937
"the physical world and
that was the hardest thing

00:02:06.937 --> 00:02:08.132
"that you had to do was

00:02:08.132 --> 00:02:09.490
to let me go."
- Yeah it was.

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:11.055
- Okay, okay.

00:02:11.055 --> 00:02:11.888
- [Theresa] "And the way
that you fixed my hair

00:02:11.888 --> 00:02:13.087
"and rubbed my face."
- I did, yeah.

00:02:13.087 --> 00:02:14.710
"after I died."
- I did.

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:15.543
- She says,

00:02:15.543 --> 00:02:16.376
"I want to thank you."

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:18.580
Your mom talks, though,

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:19.920
about her jewelry.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:21.614
So, do you have--
- Oh (beep).

00:02:21.614 --> 00:02:22.610
- Oh my Gosh!

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:23.453
- You just were telling me about

00:02:23.453 --> 00:02:24.286
her jewelry.
- You'll have to beep

00:02:24.286 --> 00:02:25.119
that out.

00:02:25.119 --> 00:02:25.952
- She says,

00:02:25.952 --> 00:02:28.750
"I want to thank you and I know."

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:29.790
- And I wear her name.

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:30.920
- Perfect.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:31.753
- Every day.

00:02:31.753 --> 00:02:32.610
I don't ever take it off.

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:34.160
- Did you take her blanket?

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:35.069
Well--
- I did!

00:02:35.069 --> 00:02:36.306
Oh my God, I stole it!

00:02:36.306 --> 00:02:37.386
(laughing)

00:02:37.386 --> 00:02:38.295
From the house!

00:02:38.295 --> 00:02:41.090
'Cause I didn't want
my stepdad to have it.

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:42.478
I stole her blanket!

00:02:42.478 --> 00:02:45.526
(laughing)

00:02:45.526 --> 00:02:47.133
- Oh my God, it's all coming out.

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:48.620
- I cuddle with it all the time.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:49.453
- [Theresa] Perfect.

00:02:49.453 --> 00:02:50.560
- That's so random.

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:51.393
- Because my--

00:02:51.393 --> 00:02:52.226
- How would

00:02:52.226 --> 00:02:53.059
she know that?
- Grandmother stitched it.

00:02:53.059 --> 00:02:54.350
- I'm freaked out.

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:55.230
- Thank you so much

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:56.527
for your gift.
- Oh, you're very welcome.

00:02:56.527 --> 00:02:57.490
- That was beautiful.
- Thank you.

00:02:57.490 --> 00:02:58.850
- I needed it, desperately.

00:02:58.850 --> 00:02:59.687
So thank you.

00:03:01.206 --> 00:03:02.233
- Oh my God.

00:03:02.233 --> 00:03:05.113
I'm here with Candice, my stylist.

00:03:06.506 --> 00:03:09.410
I mean, so when you started
talking about the mom presence,

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:10.243
Theresa, I was like,

00:03:10.243 --> 00:03:12.140
no, my mom's rocking in North Carolina,

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:12.973
she's good.

00:03:12.973 --> 00:03:13.806
Like, I was thinking in my head,

00:03:13.806 --> 00:03:15.130
but it wasn't me.

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:16.900
'Cause you kept looking off and you said,

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:17.733
well, maybe it's not you.

00:03:17.733 --> 00:03:18.810
'Cause I'm looking off and, usually,

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:20.120
'Cause it means it's not with me, right?

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:22.378
- Right.
- And your mom.

00:03:22.378 --> 00:03:23.470
You had, literally,

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:24.750
been going through this, like--

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:27.240
- Yeah, for the past year
it's been pretty brutal,

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.630
'cause she died unexpectedly.

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:31.220
So I wasn't prepared, obviously.

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:33.080
And I'd just had a baby.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:36.150
And I had serious postpartum depression.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.870
And so this last year was

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:40.790
a huge struggle not having her around

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:42.760
to be there with my newborn baby too.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:43.900
- What did that mean to you, though?

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:46.260
'Cause, that was, I felt it in the room.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:47.280
That was crazy

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:49.500
- One, the jewelry nobody knows about

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:52.750
because a family member
of mine wanted to keep it

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:54.350
and I was like, no,

00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:55.723
I'm gonna take that.

00:03:55.723 --> 00:03:56.760
It's my mother's jewelry.

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:58.060
My daughter's going to have that jewelry.

00:03:58.060 --> 00:03:58.970
So that was--
- A bit of a klepto.

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:00.258
You got the blanket, too.
- Yeah.

00:04:00.258 --> 00:04:01.330
(laughing)

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:03.440
See, that's the thing nobody knows about

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:06.870
is my grandmother crocheted
this blanket for my mother

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:09.730
and she always used it
on the couch reading

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:10.563
and stuff like that.

00:04:10.563 --> 00:04:13.386
So, I kinda just snuck it--
- Oh!

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:16.170
- Into my wardrobe case at the funeral.

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:17.840
And took it home and I was, like,

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:18.673
told my husband's family.

00:04:18.673 --> 00:04:20.430
I was like, I got this blanket.

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:21.320
But nobody, like,

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.580
I don't even, I think I
might have told his mom.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:24.520
Like, nobody knows it.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:26.370
And she was saying today, my mom was like,

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:27.660
I know you have the blanket

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:30.340
and I know that you
snuggle with it at night.

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:32.370
And that broke me, because you know,

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:33.500
I was on the fence at first.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:34.333
I don't know.

00:04:34.333 --> 00:04:36.390
But, like, nobody knows that.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:37.430
Nobody.

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:38.890
I told my husband on the phone today,

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:41.506
I was, like, it was so amazing
and also really freaky.

00:04:41.506 --> 00:04:42.339
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:42.339 --> 00:04:43.172
(audience laughing)

00:04:43.172 --> 00:04:44.853
- Because my mom is,
literally, creeping on me.

